[size=6][b]RuptureTimer — Rupture Wave Overlay for StarRupture[/b][/size]

Adds a stylish, configurable in-game overlay that shows what the Rupture Wave is doing right now, how long until it changes, and what comes next.

[b]Multiplayer-aware[/b] — the server reads the wave state and synchronises it to connected clients.

[line]

[size=5][b]Support[/b][/size]

[b]Found a bug?[/b] Report it on [url=https://github.com/AlienXAXS/StarRupture-Plugin-RuptureTimer/issues]GitHub[/url] and attach your [b]ModLoader.log[/b] (in [b]Binaries\Win64\ModLoader\Logs\[/b]).

[quote][b]If you have a question or want to discuss the mod, please join our [url=https://discord.gg/G5a4GYsvrz]Discord[/url].[/b][/quote]

[line]

[size=5][b]What It Does[/b][/size]

RuptureTimer provides an at-a-glance view of the current Rupture Wave state without having to rely solely on the vanilla HUD.

The overlay shows:

[list]
[*][b]Current state[/b] — Pre-Wave, Moving, Fadeout, Growback or Calm[/*]
[*][b]Active substage[/b] — Fire Wave, Burning, Regrowth and other substages[/*]
[*][b]Time until the next state[/b] — countdown with a progress ring[/*]
[*][b]Stage timeline[/b] — see where you currently are in the wave cycle[/*]
[*][b]Next state[/b] — see what the wave will transition into[/*]
[*][b]Multiplayer status[/b] — shows the current network role and data freshness
[/*]
[/list]
When the plugin does not have the required data, it does not guess. Unknown countdowns are displayed as [i]--:--[/i] along with the reason.

[line]

[size=5][b]Multiplayer & Server Support[/b][/size]

RuptureTimer uses the side of the game that has authority over the wave state and sends a compact snapshot to clients through the ModLoader plugin network channel.

[list]
[*][b]Solo / Offline[/b] — the client reads the wave locally and does not use networking[/*]
[*][b]Listen Server / Host[/b] — the host reads the wave and broadcasts it to connected clients[/*]
[*][b]Joined Server[/b] — the client displays the wave state received from the server[/*]
[*][b]Dedicated Server[/b] — the server reads and broadcasts the wave state; no UI is displayed
[/*]
[/list]
[b]Important:[/b] A client connected to a server without the server DLL installed will remain in its waiting state. This is intentional.

[line]

[size=5][b]Client & Server Installation[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]For players and listen-server hosts, install [b]RuptureTimer-Client[/b][/*]
[*]For dedicated servers, install [b]RuptureTimer-Server[/b][/*]
[*]Place the DLL in the game's [i]Plugins[/i] directory which is in the ModLoader directory next to [i]dwmapi.dll[/i].
[/*]
[/list]
The release ZIPs already contain a correctly named [i]Plugins\RuptureTimer.dll[/i] together with the sidecar required for automatic updates, so installing from the release ZIP is recommended.

On first launch, [i]AxRuptureTimer.ini[/i] will be generated in:

[i]<game_dir>\StarRupture\Binaries\Win64\ModLoader\Plugins\config[/i]

[b]Important:[/b] The client and server DLLs must be from the [b]same release[/b]. The network wire format is versioned, and mismatched versions will be rejected rather than decoded incorrectly.

[line]

[size=5][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Configuration can be edited through:

[i]Plugins\config\AxRuptureTimer.ini[/i]

Alternatively, use the ModLoader configuration tab. Changes are applied live and do not require a restart.

[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] — master enable/disable switch
[/*]
[*][b]ShowOverlay[/b] — show or hide the on-screen overlay
[/*]
[*][b]ToggleKey[/b] — key used to show/hide the overlay (default: F7)
[/*]
[*][b]ShowStageTimeline[/b] — show the Pre-Wave → Calm stage timeline
[/*]
[*][b]ShowProgressRing[/b] — show the countdown progress ring
[/*]
[*][b]ShowNextState[/b] — show the NEXT state line
[/*]
[*][b]ShowSubstage[/b] — show the active substage
[/*]
[*][b]ShowWavePosition[/b] — show the wave's map position while moving
[/*]
[*][b]ShowNetworkStatus[/b] — show the network role and data freshness
[/*]
[*][b]ShowTimeSinceWave[/b] — show how long the current wave has been running
[/*]
[*][b]CompactMode[/b] — display countdown only
[/*]
[*][b]LockWindow[/b] — prevent the overlay from being dragged
[/*]
[*][b]AccentByWaveType[/b] — change the accent based on Heat/Cold wave type
[/*]
[*][b]Scale[/b] — overlay size multiplier (default: 1.0, range: 0.6–2.0)
[/*]
[*][b]Opacity[/b] — overlay background opacity (default: 0.88, range: 0.15–1.0)
[/*]
[*][b]AccentPreset[/b] — 0 Signal, 1 Amber, 2 Violet, 3 Mono
[/*]
[*][b]BroadcastIntervalSeconds[/b] — server snapshot interval (default: 1.0)
[/*]
[*][b]StaleAfterSeconds[/b] — time before network data is marked stale (default: 5.0)
[/*]
[*][b]CountdownInterpolation[/b] — locally tick the countdown between server packets
[/*]
[*][b]VerboseLogging[/b] — log wave transitions and packet traffic
[/*]
[*][b]ShowDiagnosticsWindow[/b] — enable the diagnostics window
[/*]
[/list]
[b]CountdownInterpolation[/b] can be disabled for strict server-authoritative behaviour. When disabled, the countdown only displays values actually received from the server and will visibly update at the broadcast interval.

[line]

[size=5][b]Moving & Locking the Overlay[/b][/size]

The overlay is draggable by default.

A mouse cursor is available while the ModLoader window is open. Press [b]F2[/b], drag the overlay to your preferred position, then close the ModLoader window again.

Once the position is correct, set:

[i]LockWindow=true[/i]

This prevents the overlay from responding to mouse interaction.

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]StarRupture
[/*]
[*]StarRupture ModLoader
[/*]
[*]For multiplayer, the appropriate server-side plugin must be installed where required
[/*]
[/list]
[b]Note:[/b] Client and server DLLs must be from the same release.

[line]

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Overlay is waiting for data[/b] — if you are connected to a server, make sure the server has the matching RuptureTimer server DLL installed.
[/*]
[*][b]Client and server do not communicate[/b] — make sure both DLLs are from the same release.
[/*]
[*][b]Countdown appears stale[/b] — check the network status indicator and the [i]StaleAfterSeconds[/i] configuration.
[/*]
[*][b]Overlay cannot be moved[/b] — open the ModLoader window with [b]F2[/b] and make sure [i]LockWindow[/i] is disabled.
[/*]
[*][b]Need more information[/b] — enable [i]ShowDiagnosticsWindow[/i] to inspect the raw wave and network data.[/*]
[/list]

